# Case 001 — Phishing Email Investigation

## Objective
Investigate a suspicious email, identify indicators of compromise, and determine whether escalation is necessary.

## Initial Alert
- Date: Oct 22, 2026, 08:42 AM
- Alert source: Employee-reported suspicious email
- Sender:security@micros0ft-support.com
- Recipient:j.smith@company.example
- Subject:URGENT: Your Microsoft 365 Account Will Be Disabled

## Investigation Steps

| Step | Action Performed                                                   | Tool / Evidence Source                                  | Result                                                                                                            |
| ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1    | Reviewed the reported email's sender, subject, and embedded URL.   | Manual email inspection                                 | Identified suspicious email characteristics.                                                                      |
| 2    | Filtered web proxy records for `j.smith`.                          | Simulated `proxy_events.csv` logs, reviewed in ChatGPT  | Identified web activity associated with the affected user.                                                        |
| 3    | Examined HTTP requests to the suspicious domain.                   | Simulated web proxy logs                                | Identified GET and POST requests at 08:51 and 08:53 AM.                                                           |
| 4    | Reviewed outbound data volume and HTTP response codes.             | Simulated web proxy logs                                | Observed 1,438 bytes sent in a POST request; contents unknown.                                                    |
| 5    | Filtered authentication records for `j.smith`.                     | Simulated `signin_events.csv` logs, reviewed in ChatGPT | Identified authentication activity following the suspicious web requests.                                         |
| 6    | Compared sign-in timestamps, source IP addresses, and MFA results. | Simulated Microsoft Entra ID sign-in logs               | Identified a failed sign-in at 08:59 AM and a successful sign-in at 09:01 AM from the same unfamiliar IP address. |



## Indicators of Compromise
- Suspicious domains:
micros0ft-support.com — Sender domain impersonating Microsoft.
login-microsoft365.example — Suspicious website associated with the phishing email and subsequent web requests.
- URLs:
https://login-microsoft365.example/verify — URL provided in the phishing email and accessed by the user's device.
https://login-microsoft365.example/session — Destination of the POST request observed at 08:53 AM.
- IP addresses: 198.51.100.88 — Unfamiliar source IP associated with failed and successful authentication attempts for the affected account.
- File hashes:None identified. No attachments or malicious files were provided for analysis.

